    "title": "Liberty County's Cha'miya Williams turns heads yet again - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Delaney Vega ,\n4 hours ago\nBRISTOL, Fla. ( WMBB ) – Back in July, News 13 introduced a Liberty County all-star whose arm is weighed down by rings.\nShe holds five state titles across four different sports and has since been dubbed Liberty County’s sweetheart.\nFour sports. Five titles. A legacy in the making She’s done track, volleyball, weightlifting, and softball, but now Cha’miya Williams is leading the nation for girls’ varsity basketball.\nSo far this winter, the bulldogs have gone 7-3, but it’s hard to ignore Williams’ stats.\nIn the eight games she’s played this season, Williams has managed 18.1 points per game for 145 total points.\nShe averages 2.5 assists per game and 4.8 rebounds, and Williams has already had five double-doubles this year. She had an absolute career game in Liberty County’s 52-28 win over Vernon, recording 32 points, 10 rebounds, and 10 steals for her first triple-double. Williams got her second triple-double just two games after.\nBut it’s her defense that makes her a standout.\nWilliams records 9.4 steals per game, and according to MaxPreps that puts her as the No. 3 in the nation and No. 1 in Florida on this stat leaderboard.\nAnd let’s not forget this is her first year playing basketball.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to mypanhandle.com.\n3",
